\ Phase 4 slice 6a: the polymorphic array combinators, written in Sooth and
\ inlined (term-spliced) at every concrete call site, so each lowers to a tight
\ `times` loop with no per-element call and runs in constant stack.
\
\ Each is a leaf combinator: it drives a `times` loop directly and hands one
\ element to its quotation parameter per iteration. `map`/`fold` are NOT built
\ on `each`: `fold` must thread an accumulator and `map` must write each result
\ back, and this slice's quotation effects are a fixed input/output list with no
\ row variable (R28) and no captured borrow (D3), so neither can be expressed
\ through `each`'s `[ 'T -- ]` element quotation. They share the loop shape, not
\ a call.

export: each map fold ;

: each ( ['T 'N] [ 'T -- ] -- )
  | f | len >i64 | count | | arr |
  count [ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ f call ] times
  arr drop ;

: map ( ['T 'N] [ 'T -- 'T ] -- ['T 'N] )
  | f | len >i64 | count | | arr |
  count [ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ f call | v | &!arr i >usize &!> v ! ] times
  arr ;

: fold ( ['T 'N] 'A [ 'A 'T -- 'A ] -- 'A )
  | f | | acc | len >i64 | count | | arr |
  acc count [ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ f call ] times
  arr drop ;
